    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32293" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oea</span></b> , ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of Africa</i>, now <i>Tripolis</i>, Mela. 1, 7, 5; <i><span class="en">Sil. 3,
			257</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App. Mag. 17</span></i>.
			—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oeensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Œa</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civitas Oeensis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 4, 4, § 27</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Sil. 3, 257</span></i>.—<i>Plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oeenses</span></b> , ĭum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Œa</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 5,
				5, § 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 4, 50</span></i>.</div>
